  "notes": "SOLVER-SURVEY-D fragment written to loop/solver_coverage/fragments/D.json per docs/SOLVER_COVERAGE_SPEC.md section 1 (RULES schema, open-world at the value level) and the SOLVER-SURVEY-A method applied verbatim, with the D-scope additions: each row records the match/discriminator that selects the arm, the bridge entry it calls, and the kernel rule ids it reaches; every typed refusal the routing layer emits is listed (refusal_surface); each OP_CAPABILITY_MATRIX cell touched by an arm is cited (matrix_cells, all 26 cells); the door.py engine switch and op dispatch are routing rows with both occ and truck paths recorded where they diverge. Scope: truck123d/src/bd_bridge.rs (6191 lines; anchors A1=185, A2=7 hold), binding.rs, marshal.rs, facade.rs, lib.rs, python.rs; corpus/ttc/door.py; docs/OP_CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md cross-referenced only. 93 routing rows, 61 distinct unmodeled values, 113 distinct refusal labels, 26 matrix cells, 9 routing gaps, 8 refusal-surface entries. Resolved reaches into fragments A-C: C-SPLIT-TRIM-CLIP, C-SPLIT-CERTIFY-CROSSINGS, C-SPLIT-CERTIFY-OFF-LOOP, C-CLASSIFY-WINDING-NUMBER, C-CLASSIFY-SAMPLE-INSIDE, C-GATE-BEZIERLEAF1-TRY-NEW, C-GATE-POINTCERT-TRY-NEW, C-GATE-ARCCERT-TRY-NEW, C-GATE-FRAME-TRY-NEW, ADMISSION-CERTIFY-TRANSVERSE-PAIR; unresolved symbols stay exact paths (construct::volume_facts::certify_patch_form, construct::volume_facts::certify_algebraic_trim_bracket, construct::bie::ssi4::register_restricted_pair_solver, ssi_admit::register_ssi_admit_solver) because they fall outside the A-C read scopes and fragment A is not yet filed. The central W_code finding: the certified boolean dispatch (binding::boolean_dispatch -> certify_transverse_pair) and its solver registration are unreachable from the bridge/door path (RG-1/RG-2/RG-3), and the boolean product is never computed -- only the base operand is measured (RG-4). The coarse OP_CAPABILITY_MATRIX cells 2-6 read 'refuses' but the semantic route is 'facade-mirror Routed, certified product never computed'; cells 10/14/15/19 read 'certified' but the door drop-in refuses them (RG-5/RG-6). This is the refinement relation that kills the one-corpus-model-per-cell blind spot."
